From edfc0540c7d70abd0cd780587c0046a9dd0cdbfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:11:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] bitcoin: give the BLAKE2b chain its own chain_hash and
 invoice prefix

The BLAKE2b hard fork shares Bitcoin's genesis block, and BOLT 1, 2, 7
and 12 identify a chain by its genesis hash or a prefix derived from it.
A node on this chain that keeps Bitcoin's values connects to Bitcoin
nodes, merges its gossip with theirs, accepts their channel opens, and
pays or is paid with invoices that a Bitcoin wallet accepts too: the
release notes of v26.06.7-blake2b.3 name exactly this as the open
question header parsing does not settle.

The chain_hash of the network called "bitcoin" is now the id of block
961,640, the first BLAKE2b block, a fact about the chain that any node
can check with getblockhash. regtest, signet and testnet4, which have no
fixed activation block, use TaggedHash("Lightning Fork chain_hash",
genesis). The invoice prefixes are blake, blakert, tbsblake and tblake,
so an invoice is not payable on the other chain by a wallet that follows
the prefix, and a Bitcoin invoice (lnbc...) is refused here.

The genesis block id stays available as block0_hash, since the wallet
backend still reports it and the wallet stamp and BOLT 12 need it. A
unit test pins the values in the byte order getblockhash prints, so a
mistake in the little-endian arrays shows here rather than on the wire.

These are the values Lightning Fork (github.com/paulscode/lightning-fork,
an LND port) runs with on mainnet; doc/blake2b-chain-identity.md, added
in a later commit, is the shared definition.

The prefix a network had before is kept as legacy_lightning_hrp: decode
still recognises a Bitcoin invoice as one, so the user gets "Prefix bc
is not for bitcoin (expected blake)" rather than a guess at a rune, and
the bookkeeper's migration of a database from before the currency-less
accounting keeps events written with the old prefix. The BOLT 11 unit
test decodes the spec's lnbc vectors against a copy of the entry that
keeps bc, and round-trips an lnblake invoice.
